WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.920
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.040 --> 01:39.950
Episode 21:
Violin of Memories

01:50.930 --> 01:53.870
What's wrong?
- His temperature is worse than before.

01:56.600 --> 01:58.680
That's right, I might have some medicine.

02:01.570 --> 02:05.560
I think I still have Mr. Vitalis's medicine.

02:14.050 --> 02:15.840
It's not here.

02:18.090 --> 02:20.000
I must've used it all.

02:23.560 --> 02:25.870
Marcel, hang in there.

02:45.970 --> 02:47.900
It looks like he's really suffering.

02:48.700 --> 02:50.100
Is Marcel going to get better?

02:54.700 --> 02:56.400
I should get a doctor?

02:56.680 --> 03:00.120
Yes, Marcel is very sick.

03:00.140 --> 03:02.160
Please, get a doctor.

03:04.010 --> 03:06.620
A doctor? I'm not getting a doctor, they cost money.

03:07.020 --> 03:10.320
But he looks really bad.
It's not just a cold.

03:10.360 --> 03:14.250
It's his fault that he got sick.

03:17.550 --> 03:19.380
Marcel... Marcel...

03:19.890 --> 03:22.880
Get Marcel out of bed.
- No!

03:23.370 --> 03:25.030
He can't get up.

03:25.450 --> 03:28.590
Have you forgotten the rules here?

03:28.640 --> 03:30.800
No work, no food.

03:30.830 --> 03:33.890
If you can't work then you get the lash.

03:34.410 --> 03:35.890
But he can't go to work.

03:36.820 --> 03:39.160
Quit talking back.
- Stop!

03:39.200 --> 03:41.280
What?
- Yes, stop.

03:45.210 --> 03:47.000
What's with those looks?

03:47.050 --> 03:49.520
Do you want to be punished so early in the morning?

03:50.290 --> 03:51.240
Remy!

03:52.160 --> 03:54.960
I will make enough money for both me and Marcel.

03:55.110 --> 03:56.000
Huh?

03:56.080 --> 03:58.500
Then there won't be any problem, right?
- Mattia...

04:04.060 --> 04:06.510
Huh! How kind of you.

04:07.650 --> 04:10.020
I'll let him take the day off if you insist.

04:10.040 --> 04:13.630
But I won't forgive you if you don't make the money.

04:13.680 --> 04:15.690
You know what will happen, don't you?

04:20.740 --> 04:23.610
Do you think it was wise to do that?

04:23.970 --> 04:27.640
If we hadn't made that deal then Marcel couldn't take the day off.

04:27.840 --> 04:29.610
You're right, but...

04:30.040 --> 04:33.980
I can handle it. Marcel is our friend.

04:41.080 --> 04:42.510
Mattia!

04:46.670 --> 04:49.050
Will Marcel be all right by himself?

04:49.070 --> 04:51.160
I think he'll be fine.

04:53.830 --> 04:56.110
I'll go to the hospital.

04:56.130 --> 04:58.020
Hospital?
- Yes.

04:58.290 --> 05:00.560
I'll ask for a doctor to come.

05:00.920 --> 05:05.630
That's impossible. No doctor would ever come to Groussinou Avenue.

05:05.730 --> 05:07.600
And what about the money?

05:12.890 --> 05:14.880
You see, Mattia.

05:15.220 --> 05:17.840
Mr. Vitalis, who I'd been traveling with...

05:19.540 --> 05:20.840
died from an illness.

05:31.160 --> 05:35.690
If I had taken him to a doctor then, he might have survived.

05:36.100 --> 05:42.440
But I couldn't do anything for him even though I loved Mr. Vitalis so much.

05:44.970 --> 05:47.960
So I want to do my best.

05:48.050 --> 05:50.200
I want to have Marcel examined by a doctor.

05:57.070 --> 05:58.120
We can try.

05:58.140 --> 05:59.410
We have nothing to lose.

06:01.180 --> 06:02.180
Yup.

06:10.690 --> 06:13.680
A home visit? What is your address?

06:13.770 --> 06:15.560
Groussinou Avenue.

06:16.460 --> 06:18.410
Groussinou Avenue?

06:21.770 --> 06:25.990
Our doctor won't see a new patient without a referral letter,

06:26.230 --> 06:28.600
since he is a famous doctor in Paris.

06:28.910 --> 06:30.690
We'll be sure to pay.

06:31.170 --> 06:34.040
We don't have any for him now but we're sure to have it later.

06:34.370 --> 06:35.850
You don't have the money?

06:35.870 --> 06:38.030
That's why...
- Next patient, please.

06:38.290 --> 06:39.600
Yes.

06:40.520 --> 06:43.540
Remy, let's go.

06:44.770 --> 06:46.080
Please, doctor.

06:46.290 --> 06:49.000
I'm sorry, but I can't go.
I'm busy right now.

06:52.680 --> 06:54.100
No.

06:55.050 --> 06:58.240
Wait, please. I'm begging you.

06:58.270 --> 07:01.940
Remy, there aren't any doctors willing to go to Groussinou Avenue.

07:01.960 --> 07:04.240
No, I won't give up.

07:07.650 --> 07:09.200
Groussinou Avenue?

07:09.590 --> 07:11.950
I refuse to go there.

07:17.640 --> 07:20.450
Groussinou Avenue...

07:20.910 --> 07:23.790
Sorry, please try another doctor.

07:23.800 --> 07:27.290
What? Why won't you go to Groussinou Avenue?

07:27.320 --> 07:28.750
Mattia...

07:29.030 --> 07:30.550
But... Remy.

07:32.130 --> 07:34.010
Please don't be upset.

07:37.760 --> 07:39.760
Please, nurse.

07:40.100 --> 07:42.420
I don't know...

07:42.440 --> 07:44.510
What's going on?
- Oh... doctor.

07:45.080 --> 07:49.020
Please, there's a little boy who's very sick.

07:53.890 --> 07:56.280
Come in and tell me your story.

08:18.220 --> 08:20.390
Please calm down, Joli-Coeur.

08:30.120 --> 08:33.600
Doctor, how's Marcel's condition?

08:33.680 --> 08:36.870
The shot will lower his temperature.

08:37.180 --> 08:39.760
You won't have to worry once the temperature goes down.

08:39.790 --> 08:41.700
Good!

08:42.040 --> 08:44.800
But his body is very weak.

08:44.850 --> 08:49.560
You must keep him in bed and feed him a nourishing diet.

08:50.000 --> 08:51.220
We will, doctor.

08:55.250 --> 08:58.580
I will prescribe some medicine, so come and pick it up later.

08:58.600 --> 09:02.160
Yes. Thank you very much.
- Take care of him.

09:02.200 --> 09:04.880
Doctor, I'll walk with you downstairs.

09:04.900 --> 09:07.110
You will? Thank you.

09:12.650 --> 09:14.360
Remy.
- What?

09:14.740 --> 09:17.860
If our boss had been in the house, what would you have done?

09:18.410 --> 09:20.730
He told us not to get a doctor.

09:21.400 --> 09:24.460
I didn't even think about that.

09:27.670 --> 09:30.630
Huh! That's just like you, Remy.

09:36.730 --> 09:39.120
I'm happy for you, Marcel.

09:44.490 --> 09:47.430
Thank you very much, doctor.

11:02.050 --> 11:04.460
Mattia! Mattia!

11:05.360 --> 11:07.760
Mattia!

11:07.780 --> 11:08.880
I'm coming!

11:19.530 --> 11:22.440
It's great that Marcel's fever has gone down.

11:22.720 --> 11:26.720
But we have to make enough money to pay for the doctor's visit and the medicine.

11:26.750 --> 11:28.200
I have a good job.

11:28.390 --> 11:31.920
It's a tough job, but it brings in a lot of money. I'm going there.

11:32.310 --> 11:34.010
I'll do my best, too.

11:38.440 --> 11:40.760
Capi and Joli-Coeur are saying they will do their best, too.

11:41.140 --> 11:42.130
All right.

11:42.290 --> 11:43.760
Let's meet in the park in the evening.

11:45.730 --> 11:47.840
Come on! Move forward!

11:55.890 --> 11:57.440
Here you go.

11:59.800 --> 12:01.290
Damn it.

12:06.030 --> 12:09.080
What's wrong? Your legs are kind of staggering.

12:14.930 --> 12:17.880
Man, it's hot.
- All right, take a break.

12:26.580 --> 12:27.950
Mattia...

12:29.070 --> 12:31.460
Mattia, what's wrong?

12:31.700 --> 12:35.460
Oh... We got a doctor to examine Marcel.

12:35.600 --> 12:37.690
He said once his fever goes down, he'll be fine.

12:37.710 --> 12:41.400
A doctor? Even though we didn't have the money?

12:41.700 --> 12:45.060
Yeah, so I need to make money for the medicine and the visit.

12:45.090 --> 12:47.400
So that's why you're doing this hard job.

12:47.690 --> 12:49.400
Right...

13:01.450 --> 13:05.050
Mattia isn't it easier doing <i>that</i> ?

13:05.270 --> 13:07.430
What?
- Over there.

13:09.600 --> 13:12.080
Rich people.
We could make some fast money.

13:12.370 --> 13:13.070
No!

13:13.620 --> 13:15.830
I decided I'm not stealing anymore.

13:15.860 --> 13:19.110
Just once more, for Marcel.

13:19.150 --> 13:24.080
No! You said you didn't want to steal either.

13:24.420 --> 13:27.070
All right, all right.
Get your hands off me.

13:28.010 --> 13:30.070
What's with you all of a sudden?

13:30.200 --> 13:33.080
Sorry... But don't say that again.

13:34.680 --> 13:36.980
Okay. I'll never say it again.

13:37.000 --> 13:38.590
It's a promise, man to man.

13:39.030 --> 13:41.080
Huh! You cheeky guy...

13:43.670 --> 13:45.140
Hang in there, Mattia.

13:45.270 --> 13:46.330
Let me help you.

13:46.700 --> 13:49.010
Then, I have a favor to ask.

13:49.980 --> 13:53.110
Buy some milk with this money and bring it to Marcel.

13:53.290 --> 13:55.300
He has to have nutritious food.

13:55.700 --> 13:56.800
Okay.

13:57.580 --> 13:59.970
Mattia! Mattia!

14:00.220 --> 14:01.660
All right, I'll leave it to you.

14:03.390 --> 14:05.520
He's changed, that guy.

14:07.310 --> 14:08.800
All thanks to Remy, eh?

14:12.870 --> 14:16.350
10, 11, 12, 13, 14...

14:16.370 --> 14:19.560
14 sous, that's not nearly enough.

14:20.900 --> 14:22.960
All right, we have to work harder.

14:26.120 --> 14:28.680
Mattia must be working hard, I guess.

14:49.080 --> 14:51.870
Here's some milk. It's delicious.

14:52.290 --> 14:54.760
Slowly, slowly.

14:59.100 --> 15:00.840
Thank you, Ricardo.

15:01.020 --> 15:01.960
It's very good.

15:02.210 --> 15:05.070
You'll get better soon, Marcel.

15:08.270 --> 15:09.960
Listen, like I told you before,

15:10.750 --> 15:16.560
Mattia has been doing a very hard job for Marcel. We can do something, too.

15:16.630 --> 15:17.840
Yeah.
- Yeah.

15:18.970 --> 15:21.850
We're all friends, aren't we?

15:21.890 --> 15:25.780
Yes! That's right!
- We'll all do our best, won't we?

15:34.870 --> 15:37.450
We have to be quick.
We don't have much time.

15:38.530 --> 15:41.400
I don't have much time, either.

16:02.570 --> 16:04.750
What are you doing, Mattia?

16:04.760 --> 16:08.220
I know. We don't have a lot of time, right?

16:19.240 --> 16:21.000
24 sous.

16:22.230 --> 16:25.200
What should I do? This isn't even close to enough.

16:25.890 --> 16:26.960
Remy!

16:30.710 --> 16:32.320
Sorry, Mattia.

16:33.460 --> 16:36.340
I only made 24 sous.

16:36.750 --> 16:38.420
It's just one of those days.

16:38.520 --> 16:41.740
No one wants to go out on such a hot day.

16:42.460 --> 16:44.100
I made 45 sous.

16:44.720 --> 16:46.770
We can pay for the visit with this.

16:47.860 --> 16:49.540
But what about the medicine?

16:49.580 --> 16:51.520
Marcel needs the medicine.

16:53.780 --> 16:58.080
I'm sorry, I should have worked harder.

16:59.130 --> 17:00.030
Remy...

17:03.770 --> 17:05.030
Remy!

17:06.870 --> 17:10.540
Don't forget to put our money into account.

17:12.710 --> 17:17.170
Guys, you'll be badly punished by the boss if you give all your money.

17:17.220 --> 17:19.310
That's right. You'll be in big trouble.

17:19.830 --> 17:21.810
I don't mind as long as everyone's with me.

17:21.840 --> 17:23.920
Me, too.
- Me too.

17:23.920 --> 17:26.880
Me, too. I'm not scared.
- Me, too.

17:30.050 --> 17:31.020
We're short.

17:31.470 --> 17:34.600
We're still short even with all the money you guys collected.

17:34.630 --> 17:36.030
What do you mean?

17:37.330 --> 17:40.180
Mr. Vitalis's medicine was very expensive.

17:40.200 --> 17:42.290
So I don't think this is enough.

17:42.710 --> 17:47.620
Then, we can't do anything for Marcel?

17:48.410 --> 17:49.210
Mattia.

17:57.320 --> 17:59.810
Huh... It's no use.

18:06.100 --> 18:07.060
Lise...

18:07.120 --> 18:09.400
Why do you have that violin?

18:09.560 --> 18:12.640
It seemed interesting, so I brought it with me.

18:12.890 --> 18:15.600
Don't be mad at me, big brother Mattia.

18:16.540 --> 18:17.760
Mattia...

18:35.850 --> 18:37.680
Quiet, Joli-Coeur.

19:19.000 --> 19:20.130
Mattia!

19:20.520 --> 19:24.220
That was great! You're a genius, Mattia.
- Remy...

19:24.600 --> 19:25.220
I...

19:26.340 --> 19:28.560
That was awesome!

19:28.960 --> 19:30.270
That was great!

19:33.990 --> 19:36.690
Yes! Yes! Thank you very much!

19:37.530 --> 19:43.440
It's been quite a long time since I heard something that touched my soul like that.

19:43.860 --> 19:45.190
Here's a token of my appreciation.

19:45.630 --> 19:48.780
Treasure that talent of yours.

19:53.260 --> 19:54.510
A gold coin.

20:01.250 --> 20:03.350
Here, drink this.

20:04.180 --> 20:05.010
It's good.

20:06.080 --> 20:09.030
Good.
- Now he'll get better soon.

20:09.070 --> 20:10.760
It's all thanks to Mattia.

20:18.490 --> 20:20.730
Wow... It's beautiful, isn't it?

20:27.420 --> 20:30.020
That was the first time...
- Huh?

20:31.140 --> 20:34.680
that I worked so hard for somebody else.

20:35.050 --> 20:36.370
The first time.

20:37.110 --> 20:39.790
Your violin playing was wonderful.

20:40.090 --> 20:41.950
It was really wonderful.

20:42.490 --> 20:44.260
Did you learn how to play before?

20:51.020 --> 20:53.900
You like that violin a lot, don't you?

20:55.170 --> 20:58.170
It was Mr. Vitalis's violin.

20:59.230 --> 21:02.560
My most loved person's violin.

21:04.050 --> 21:05.950
I want to give it to you.

21:06.690 --> 21:07.950
Please take it.

21:08.340 --> 21:10.410
But it's important to you, isn't it?

21:11.480 --> 21:16.600
It's all right. Mr. Vitalis will be happy to have someone play his violin.

21:16.640 --> 21:18.670
From now on, it'll be your violin.

21:19.850 --> 21:22.800
My violin?
- Yes.

21:24.970 --> 21:25.600
But...

21:26.210 --> 21:28.300
I want you to play it, Mattia.

21:36.170 --> 21:37.650
Thank you, Remy.

21:37.660 --> 21:41.670
I will treasure it.
- I'm glad!

21:39.400 --> 21:47.700
Try to love yourself more

21:48.740 --> 21:57.980
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

21:58.290 --> 22:07.400
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:07.960 --> 22:18.900
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:19.310 --> 22:29.230
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:29.370 --> 22:38.870
From the future that gives us our fate

22:39.130 --> 22:48.420
Try to seek for them more

22:48.770 --> 22:52.660
Give your heart to

22:52.710 --> 23:05.680
That person who is also seeking you

23:20.900 --> 23:23.570
What are you doing here?

23:23.780 --> 23:26.240
There's trouble! Come on everyone!

23:26.410 --> 23:29.430
Remy's been trapped in the coal mine.
- What?

23:31.440 --> 23:35.440
<i>Surviving the Underground</i>

23:31.440 --> 23:35.440
Next time:
